    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of a hand (又) climbing a cliff (厂). Based on original meaning \"pull\", later extended to \"turn around\", \"oppose\"."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "覆也。从又，厂反形。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "STEDT compares it to Proto-Sino-Tibetan *par (“to trade; to buy; to sell”), from which Tibetan ཕར (phar, “interest (on money); exchange”) is derived.\nCognate with 販 (OC *pans, “to trade”), which is an exoactive of 反 (OC *panʔ, *pʰan, “to return, lit. to make someone return”) (Schuessler, 2007).\n番 (OC *pʰan, “a turn; a time”) is the iterative of 反 (OC *panʔ, *pʰan)."
    }
  ],
